  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">We Participate</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the Jordanian non-profit organization Forearms of Change, which was founded to serve and meet the needs of vulnerable communities (Female Sex workers, Men who have sex with Men, People Who Use Drugs, LGBTQI-people living with HIV and their partners). We Participate&quot; is a gender-based violence (GBV) project with the primary objective of mitigating GBV towards vulnerable communities in Jordan. These communities encompass the LGBTQI community, Female Sex Workers, Men who Have Sex with Men, People Who Use Drugs, and People Living with HIV, representing various nationalities, backgrounds, and age groups. 

This project is structured as a service provision project, focusing on delivering tailored protection services to GBV survivors from the identified vulnerable communities. These services are designed to address the specific needs and circumstances of the survivors, empowering them to navigate and overcome the challenges and difficulties they encounter in their lives. The project aims to &quot;Contribute to limiting GBV in Jordan towards Vulnerable Communities, ensuring that Diverse Vulnerable Communities receive adequate social protection and health services in Jordan.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
